{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implemented and pushed for review: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1035. Deviation notes: (1) plan_review/__init__.py sat at 799 LOC against the 800 hard CI cap, so both reuse paths (existing idempotent_reuse + new verdict_reuse) were extracted along the existing call seam into a new plan_review/reuse.py (152 LOC); __init__ now calls reuse.idempotent_reuse / reuse.verdict_reuse. (2) tests placed at tests/unit/test_plan_review_reuse.py (self-contained repo fixture) rather than the plan's tests/llm/ path, which does not exist as a test tier; conventions mirrored from tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_block_loop_remediation.py. 7 new tests green; existing gate/idempotence suites (89 + 47 tests), lint, typecheck all pass locally."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785397639487646001,"uuid":"b5156737-b988-4aad-8d2f-8b8a16b14c48"}